  "body": "## What changed\n\n**#672 step 1** (part of #621's plasma research): `sim::verify::plasma`, the laws that replace the gouge and collision checks for a 2D plasma through-cut. Based on main, with no dependency on #674 or #670.\n\n**What it judges:** a neutral `PlasmaProgram`:\n- the kerf;\n- the cuts in cut order, each the torch-on polyline with its contour id, inner/outer and parent outer;\n- the rapid into each cut.\n\nSo it reads the CL's torch records (#670's `TorchOn { contour, inner, parent }` / `TorchOff`) and nothing of the operation's internals.\n\n| Law | Verdict | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Cut order:** an inner contour cut after the outer that frees its part | **refusal** | plain plasma practice; the part drops before its holes |\n| **Kerf crossing:** a cut within one kerf of an earlier cut's centre line | warning | LinuxCNC Plasma Primer §12 (THC dive into an open kerf) |\n| **Tip-up:** a rapid across a part already cut free | warning | Tormach 1300PL manual UM10720 §1.4.2, §4.12.8 |\n| **Malformed:** a non-positive or non-finite kerf, a NaN point, a cut with no path | **refusal** | Prime Directive |\n\n**Not yet wired.** Step 2 builds the `PlasmaProgram` from the plasma op's CL torch records once #670 lands, blocks the post on a refusal, and updates the machine check's `notes` (#674) to say these laws judge plasma ops.\n\n## How tested\n\n- **New `crates/sim/tests/plasma_laws.rs`, 5/5.** Each law is tripped by one fixture and passed by another:\n  - a plate with a hole, hole-first (clean) versus outline-first (refused);\n  - two outlines 1 mm apart at a 1.5 mm kerf (warned) versus 5 mm apart (clear);\n  - a rapid over a freed part (warned) versus around it (clear);\n  - the malformed kerf, point and path cases.\n- **`scripts/gate.sh quick`:** the sim suites pass.\n- **Clippy** on sim with `-D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe CL reader and verdict wiring (step 2, after #670). The 2D gouge (the kerf band against the part's section) needs the part's 2D section from the op, also step 2.\n\nChangelog: none (internal: plasma laws, not yet wired)\n\nRefs #672\nRefs #621\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
